.TH IMPROV-IMPORT-SQL 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-import\-sql \- Import a SQLite query into a new SQL\-backed input measure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov import\-sql\fR [OPTIONS] <db> <source.sqlite> <measure\-id> <measure\-name> <SELECT> <value\-col> <dim\-col:cat\-id:cat\-name>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a SQLite query into a new SQL\-backed input measure.
.PP
Each dimension spec maps a result column to a category (its distinct values become items); the value column holds the numbers. Re\-run the query with refresh\-sql. Example: improv import\-sql m.db sales.db 100 Revenue "SELECT t,p,r FROM sales" r t:1:Time p:2:Product
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR \fI<policy>\fR [default: manual]
When serve\-refresh re\-runs it: manual, on\-load or interval:SECS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIsource.sqlite\fR>
The SQLite database to query
.TP
<\fImeasure\-id\fR>
The new measure\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fImeasure\-name\fR>
The new measure\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fISELECT\fR>
The query
.TP
<\fIvalue\-col\fR>
The result column holding the values
.TP
<\fIdim\-col:cat\-id:cat\-name\fR>
COLUMN:CATEGORY\-ID:CATEGORY\-NAME: a column, and the category its distinct values become items of
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
